# MF Overhaul 0.4.7: SINGLE-VARIABLE TEST. 0.4.6 cut the burst launch spread to 15 % and the columns got TALLER and denser (80-100 m),
#   so the rise is not the launch velocity. The other cell 0.4.6 changed on the smoke rows was c13 slot 3 (0.15/0.2 -> 0.06), assumed
#   to be size growth; if it is velocity damping instead, lowering it let the puffs keep climbing, which matches the screenshot.
#   Test: slot 3 -> 1.2 on the three burst-smoke rows, nothing else. Compact low cloud -> slot 3 is damping. Tiny puffs that never
#   grow -> slot 3 is the growth fraction (then revert to 0.15).
# 3 operations
row~|parts_desc|smoke_expl|c13=v:22;0.35;0.05;1.2
row~|parts_desc|smoke_expl_big|c13=v:28;0.35;0.05;1.2
row~|parts_desc|smoke_bomb|c13=v:34;0.35;0.05;1.2
